{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelLaplace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelLaplace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelResummation","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Gamma.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.DominatedConvergence"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelSum_eq_tsum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelSum_eq_tsum","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelLaplace.lean#L148-L171","doc":"**Borel-summation regularity / consistency.** When the series converges\nabsolutely at `z` (`∑ₙ |aₙ||z|ⁿ < ∞`), the Borel sum equals the ordinary\nsum: `∫₀^∞ e^{−t} φ(z t) dt = ∑' n, aₙ zⁿ`. Proved by `integral_tsum` — the\nabsolute-convergence hypothesis is exactly the finiteness of the dominating\n`∑ₙ ∫ ‖·‖` — with each term recovered by `laplace_borel_term`. Sorry-free;\nthe divergent (Gevrey-1) case, where this fails, is the open Watson gap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelSum","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelLaplace.lean#L142-L146","doc":"The **Borel sum** of `a` at `z`: the Laplace transform of the pointwise Borel\ntransform `φ(w) = ∑' n, borelCoeff a n · wⁿ` along `ℝ₊`,\n`∫₀^∞ e^{−t} φ(z t) dt`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.lintegral_enorm_borelIntegrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.lintegral_enorm_borelIntegrand","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelLaplace.lean#L135-L140","doc":"`∫⁻₀^∞ ‖e^{−t}(borelCoeff a n)(z t)ⁿ‖ₑ dt = ENNReal.ofReal (|aₙ| |z|ⁿ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.integral_norm_borelIntegrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.integral_norm_borelIntegrand","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelLaplace.lean#L116-L133","doc":"`∫₀^∞ ‖e^{−t}(borelCoeff a n)(z t)ⁿ‖ dt = |aₙ| |z|ⁿ`. The `|borelCoeff a n|`\nand the `n!` from `laplace_pow_eq_factorial` cancel to `|aₙ|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.integrableOn_borelIntegrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.integrableOn_borelIntegrand","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelLaplace.lean#L103-L114","doc":"Integrability of the `n`-th Borel integrand `e^{−t}·(borelCoeff a n)(z t)ⁿ`\non `Ioi 0`: it is the constant `borelCoeff a n · zⁿ` times Euler's\nconvergent `e^{−t} tⁿ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.laplace_borel_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.laplace_borel_term","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelLaplace.lean#L56-L72","doc":"**Per-term Borel recovery**: the `n`-th term of the Borel transform,\n`(aₙ/n!)(z t)ⁿ`, Laplace-integrates back to the `n`-th term `aₙ zⁿ` of the\noriginal series. The Borel division by `n!` and the Laplace multiplication\nby `n!` (from `laplace_pow_eq_factorial`) cancel exactly — the mechanism of\nBorel resummation, term by term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.laplace_pow_eq_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.laplace_pow_eq_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelLaplace.lean#L42-L54","doc":"**The Laplace term-wise engine**: `∫₀^∞ e^{−t} tⁿ dt = n!`. Euler's Gamma\nintegral at the natural argument `s = n + 1`, with `Real.rpow` collapsed to\nthe monoid power on `t`. This is the single analytic fact underneath Borel\nresummation — every `n!` that Borel division removed is restored by this\nLaplace integral. ","signatureChunk":0}]}